# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CourseScope — deployment configuration (reference)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The live values for v1.0.0 are in `.env.production`. This file documents every
# variable for anyone deploying elsewhere. Copy to `.env` (or set these in your
# host's environment) before building.
#
# Every variable is OPTIONAL: the app builds and runs with none of them set,
# and degrades honestly rather than pretending a feature is wired up.
#
# Vite inlines VITE_* variables at BUILD time, into a PUBLIC bundle. Changing
# one means rebuilding, and nothing secret may ever go in one.

# --- Where "Report an issue" sends people -----------------------------------
# Set ONE of these. A form is preferred: it can validate and route, and it does
# not publish an address. With neither set, the report UI still works but offers
# only "Copy report" and says plainly that there is nowhere to submit to.
#
# VITE_FEEDBACK_URL=https://example.org/course-data-issue
# VITE_FEEDBACK_EMAIL=course-data@example.org

# --- Canonical URL for metadata --------------------------------------------
# The URL the site is actually served from, with no trailing slash. Used for
# the canonical link and Open Graph URL. Leave unset rather than guess: a wrong
# canonical URL tells crawlers the wrong page is authoritative.
#
# VITE_SITE_URL=https://example.org

# --- Social preview image ---------------------------------------------------
# Absolute URL of the preview card. The image ships as dist/social-preview.png;
# point this at wherever your host serves it. Unset means text-only share cards.
#
# VITE_OG_IMAGE_URL=https://example.org/social-preview.png

# --- Base path --------------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed when serving from a subdirectory (e.g. GitHub Pages project
# sites). Must have a leading and trailing slash. Defaults to "./" (relative).
#
# VITE_BASE_PATH=/coursescope/
